hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"17935","al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Sulayman narrated to us that al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to them, from Amr ibn so-and-so al-Ansari, he said, While he was walking with his waist-wrapper trailing, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) caught up with him, holding the forelock of himself and saying, O Allah, Your servant, son of Your servant, son of Your bondwoman. Amr said, So I said, O Messenger of Allah, I am a man with thin shanks. So he said, O Amr, Allah Almighty has made well everything He created. O Amr. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) struck with four fingers of his right hand below the knee of Amr and said, O Amr, this is the place of the waist-wrapper. Then he raised it, then placed it below the second, and said, O Amr, this is the place of the waist-wrapper."
